      "title": "Simulation Manager",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Simulation Manager Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Simulation Manager Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Simulation Manager Department 0090 - Nursing Position Number 986830 Requisition No. S02832 Salary Range/Pay Rate $61,728 - $69,438 annually Benefits of Working at Oakland University Oakland University offers competitive salaries and an excellent benefit program including a comprehensive medical plan with low contribution amounts for our employees, dental and vision plans at no cost for our employees, generous paid time off plans, a generous University contribution to our 403(b) retirement plan, tuition assistance for our employees and dependents, free access to our Campus Recreation Center and workout facilities, and flexible work schedules and wellness programs. These are current benefit levels subject to future changes. Oakland University offers a strong, University-wide commitment to diversity, equity and inclusion, which has garnered national recognition as a top workplace for LGBTQ+ community members; national recognition as a safe workplace, and consistent top ranking for support services to U.S. Military veteran students. Employee Group/Grade AP Band P Job Category Administrative-Professional Work Schedule FT/Reg (40 hours) Shift/Days This is a full time, day shift position, Monday through Friday, with occasional weekends and evenings. First consideration will be given to those who apply by October 6, 2026. Pay Schedule Month Number of Hrs./Wk. 40 hours per week Position Information Position Information Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Nursing or an equivalent combination of education and/or experience. A minimum of two (2) years of experience in simulation education. Strong knowledge of clinical skills training, including the use of standardized patients and nursing simulation technology in a clinical education setting. Ability to interact and communicate professionally and effectively with a diverse range of individuals, including physicians, faculty, students, patients, standardized patients, and the general public. Excellent organizational and analytical skills, along with strong oral and written communication abilities. Capable of effectively conveying information to others. Desired Qualifications Experience in clinical and patient care settings. Developed and implemented clinical skills training curricula. Experience in creating and executing standardized patient exercises for training and assessment. Experience interacting with students in a post-secondary educational environment. Possesses knowledge of specific terminology related to the unit and program area. Experience in developing and implementing simulation activities, as well as in selecting and maintaining simulation equipment and learning management software. All Qualifications Unless otherwise required by an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Position Details Position Purpose Reporting directly to the Director of Nursing Laboratories, the Simulation Manager will provide comprehensive operational, technical, and instructional support for the School of Nursing’s simulation program. This role is responsible for the coordination, execution, and continuous improvement of simulation-based learning activities to ensure consistent, high-quality experiential education aligned with curricular goals. As the simulation program expands in scope, volume, and interdisciplinary use, the Simulation Coordinator plays a critical role in supporting faculty, students, and institutional priorities by managing daily operations, simulation technology, and assessment processes Job Open Date 09/23/2026 Job Close Date Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a member of the Oakland University Administrative-Professional Group? Yes No No Response * Describe your experience with clinical simulation. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your experience in nursing clinical education. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
