      "title": "Sports Dietitian",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Sports Dietitian Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Sports Dietitian Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Sports Dietitian Department 2836 - Athletics Administration Position Number E44252 Requisition No. TC06547 Salary Range/Pay Rate 50.00 hr. Benefits of Working at Oakland University No benefits are associated with this position. Employee Group/Grade Casual Job Category Casual /Temporary Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule Casual (19hrs or less, No Benefits ) Shift/Days Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. 19 Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 10/26/2026 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. n/a Minimum Qualifications Registered dietitian with Bachelor’s degree. Use of language and tools that foster a healthy body image environment. Must be able to work flexible hours including evenings and weekends. Desired Qualifications Master’s Degree. CSSD Certification. 1-2 years sports nutrition experience. Collegiate sports nutrition experience Knowledge of NCAA rules regarding dietary supplements and third-party certifications Position Purpose Oakland University Athletics is a Division I program committed to academic and athletic excellence. Our Athletic Department is looking for a highly organized, driven and detail oriented individual to fill the position of Sports Dietitian. This position reports directly to the Associate Athletic Director for Academic and Sport Performance. The Sports Dietitian will be responsible for assisting all varsity sports programs with sport nutrition needs, working in conjunction with Sports Medicine and Strength and Conditioning. This position should have a knowledge of NCAA rules as it pertains to assigned job duties and the scope of employment. Job Duties Conduct one-on-one nutrition assessments and provide follow-up with DI student athletes on topics including, but not limited to performance enhancement, hydration, weight gain, weigh loss/body composition changes, safe supplementation, blood work, injury prevention and healing, campus dining, travel, food allergies/sensitivities, and disordered eating behaviors. Conduct sport specific team nutrition education sessions. Communicate consistently with athletic trainers and members of the sports medicine and strength and conditioning staff and team managers. Collaborate with sport coaches. Work can be completed in person and/or virtually. Job Open Date 10/09/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
