    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/39180": {
      "title": "Program Director for Principal Gifts",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Program Director for Principal Gifts Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Program Director for Principal Gifts Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Program Director for Principal Gifts Department 7431 - Campaign & Stewardship Position Number 986470 Requisition No. S02835 Salary Range/Pay Rate $85,850 - $96,589 annually Benefits of Working at Oakland University Oakland University offers competitive salaries and an excellent benefit program including a comprehensive medical plan with low contribution amounts for our employees, dental and vision plans at no cost for our employees, generous paid time off plans, a generous University contribution to our 403(b) retirement plan, tuition assistance for our employees and dependents, free access to our Campus Recreation Center and workout facilities, and flexible work schedules and wellness programs. These are current benefit levels subject to future changes. Employee Group/Grade AP Band S Job Category Administrative-Professional Work Schedule FT/Reg (40 hours) Shift/Days This is a full-time position. First consideration will be given to those who apply by September 28, 2026. Pay Schedule Month Number of Hrs./Wk. 40 Position Information Position Information Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree in Communications, Business, Marketing or a related area or an equivalent combination of education and/or experience. A minimum of four (4) years of experience in advancement, donor relations, engagement, strategic communications, executive engagement, higher education, or a related field Knowledge of fundraising processes, strategy, and relationship management tactics and the role that strategic engagement opportunities play in advancing donor relationships. . Ability to establish, maintain and strengthen relationships with signiﬁcant donors. Must be an outstanding project manager, and able to balance complex projects with competing priorities across multiple stakeholders and ability to work collegially and interact effectively with a diverse constituency. Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, including proposal writing, executive correspondence, donor communications, and presentation development Demonstrated experience supporting senior executives, boards, trustees, or volunteer leaders. Experience coordinating high-profile meetings, events, visits, and relationship-building activities involving senior leaders and external stakeholders. This position requires a high level of phone communication, very limited travel and the ability to work events in the evenings and weekends. Desired Qualifications Master’s degree. Ability to translate academic, research, healthcare, and institutional priorities into compelling philanthropic opportunities. Ability to establish priorities and ensure accountability across teams. All Qualifications Unless otherwise required by an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Position Details Position Purpose The Program Director for Principal Gifts reports to the Assistant Vice President of Strategic Philanthropy in University Advancement and works directly with the Office of the President for Oakland University. This position plays a key role in managing the daily and strategic operational functions for the Principal Gifts team through high level strategy and execution of complex donor engagement mapping, managing timelines, and managing considerations associated with high-level donor engagement activities that deepen affinity to the University. This position ensures that briefings, agendas, and all preparation materials are available and communicated in an effective manner. This position will also support strategic, customized prospect communication including writing proposals, executive summaries, white papers and other correspondence. This position will work collaboratively with all levels of the organization, especially Prospect Management and Research, to maintain the organization and oversight of the full principal gift prospect list. Responsibilities include convening campus partners and advising the team on the development of successful coordinated strategies aimed to maximize the life-time engagement and support of these prospects. This position plays a critical role in the coordination of Presidential donor activity and ensuring engagements are thoughtful, intentional, and purposeful. The Program Director will give updates on these prospects and their strategy, next-steps, and needs to the advancement leadership team and the President. The position will coordinate the president’s regional donor engagement and prepare for off – site donor visits and travel. Job Open Date 09/15/2026 Job Close Date Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a member of the Oakland University Administrative-Professional Group? Yes No No Response Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Writing Sample 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/39169": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Advising",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Assistant Director of Advising Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Assistant Director of Advising Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Assistant Director of Advising Department 0090 - Nursing Position Number 988546 Requisition No. S02825 Salary Range/Pay Rate $61,728 - $69,438 annually Benefits of Working at Oakland University Oakland University offers competitive salaries and an excellent benefit program including a comprehensive medical plan with low contribution amounts for our employees, dental and vision plans at no cost for our employees, generous paid time off plans, a generous University contribution to our 403(b) retirement plan, tuition assistance for our employees and dependents, free access to our Campus Recreation Center and workout facilities, and flexible work schedules and wellness programs. These are current benefit levels subject to future changes. Employee Group/Grade AP Band P Job Category Administrative-Professional Work Schedule FT/Reg (40 hours) Shift/Days This is a full time, day shift position, Monday through Friday, with occasional weekends and evenings. First consideration will be given to those who apply by September 15, 2026. Pay Schedule Month Number of Hrs./Wk. 40 Position Information Position Information Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree or equivalent combination of education and/or experience. A minimum of three (3) years experience in academic counseling or advising plus three (3) years experience in a supervisory role of personnel, including hiring and training. Experience in budget management. Excellent leadership, organization and analytical skills. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to communicate effectively with others. Desired Qualifications Knowledge of university academic policy and curricula. Five years of collegiate academic advising experience. All Qualifications Unless otherwise required by an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Position Details Position Purpose As the School of Nursing ( SON ) has continued to grow, so has the number of advisers and programs. The Assistant Director of Advising will be responsible for the day-to-day operational needs for advising services. The Assistant Director will be instrumental in developing and supporting targeted initiatives aimed at enhancing nursing-specific orientations, registration, academic progress, and overall academic success. In addition to managing an advising caseload, the Assistant Director will focus on increasing the retention and success of both graduate and undergraduate nursing students. The Assistant Director will support the Director in leading initiatives to enhance our advising services, ensuring that all students receive personalized guidance throughout their academic journey. Job Open Date 09/01/2026 Job Close Date Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a member of the Oakland University Administrative-Professional Group? Yes No No Response * Please describe your academic and career advising experience. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your overall leadership and supervision style including examples that demonstrate your behavior. (Open Ended Question) * Describe how you have used problem-solving skills in a multi-focused office, including interactions with co-workers,students, faculty and external clientele. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
