    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/39145": {
      "title": "Director of Accounting Services",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Director of Accounting Services Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Director of Accounting Services Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Director of Accounting Services Department 2445 - Accounting Office Position Number 992454 Requisition No. S02843 Salary Range/Pay Rate $120,500 - $139,750 annually Benefits of Working at Oakland University Oakland University offers competitive salaries and an excellent benefit program including a comprehensive medical plan with low contribution amounts for our employees, dental and vision plans at no cost for our employees, generous paid time off plans, a generous University contribution to our 403(b) retirement plan, tuition assistance for our employees and dependents, free access to our Campus Recreation Center and workout facilities, and flexible work schedules and wellness programs. These are current benefit levels subject to future changes. Oakland University offers a strong, University-wide commitment to diversity, equity and inclusion, which has garnered national recognition as a top workplace for LGBTQ+ community members; national recognition as a safe workplace, and consistent top ranking for support services to U.S. Military veteran students. Employee Group/Grade AP Band U Job Category Administrative-Professional Work Schedule FT/Reg (40 hours) Shift/Days This is a full-time position. First consideration will be given to those who apply by October 8, 2026. Pay Schedule Month Number of Hrs./Wk. 40 Position Information Position Information Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Accounting or an equivalent combination of education and/or experience. A minimum of six (6) years of professional accounting experience, plus two (2) years of supervisory/management experience. Proficiency with personal computers, spreadsheet software applications, and enterprise wide automated financial systems. Experience with and an aptitude for advanced technical systems and reporting. Excellent organizational and analytical skills. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to communicate effectively with others. Desired Qualifications Master’s degree in Business Administration, Accounting or related field. Professional certification (e.g. C.M.A., C.P.A.). Database management experience. Banner experience. Higher education experience, Tax research and preparation experience. Strong technical ability and experience. All Qualifications Unless otherwise required by an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Position Details Position Purpose Oversee and manage the Central Accounting functions of the University including financial system management, preparation of audited financial statements, and tax compliance. More specifically, the Director of Accounting Services is very broad and complex. Key areas of responsibility include financial reporting, overseeing the financial statement preparation and coordination with the external audit firm. This is a highly visible position that requires a vast amount of technical knowledge and experience. This position requires a Certified Public Accounting ( CPA ) certification. Requires in depth knowledge of GASB pronouncements and implementation procedures. This position manages the banner finance module and security access to it, including being a finance data steward. System integrity is key to all internal control systems and this position ensures compliance is maintained. This position trains the entire campus on financial reporting and compliance. The federal single audit is managed by this position which is a complex compliance audit. The NCAA agreed upon procedures is managed by this position. Annual negotiation of the Federal fringe benefit rates are managed by this role. This position manages banking relationships and oversees transaction processes including positive pay, cash management, ACH , wires, etc. This position is a key member of the Financial Performance Review committee to provide oversight and guidance to business units on campus. This position is a senior financial expert and advisor to leadership and the campus community. Job Open Date 09/25/2026 Job Close Date Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a member of the Oakland University Administrative-Professional Group? Yes No No Response Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/39144": {
      "title": "Visiting Instructor of Mathematics and Statistics",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Visiting Instructor of Mathematics and Statistics Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Visiting Instructor of Mathematics and Statistics Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For full consideration, applications should be submitted online at https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37798 by June 12, 2026. Applications should include a cover letter outlining your teaching interests and relevant experience, current curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, copies of graduate transcripts. In addition, names and contact information for three letters of recommendation must be provided. The application system will contact the letter writers via email and provide them with instructions for uploading their letters. The search will remain open until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Visiting Instructor of Mathematics and Statistics Department 1038 - Mathematical & Statistics Requisition No. 0000825 Job Description Summary The Department of Mathematics and Statistics at Oakland University invites applications for at least one Visiting Instructor position. The successful candidate will primarily be responsible for supporting the department’s teaching mission through the instruction of foundational undergraduate courses (including introductory mathematics and statistics). The standard teaching load for this position is three courses per semester (3+3). In addition to teaching excellence, the Visiting Instructor is required to fulfill service duties that advance the department’s mission. These may include assisting with student success initiatives. As this is a teaching-intensive appointment, there are no research requirements or expectations for scholarly publication. Minimum Qualifications Candidates should possess a Ph.D. in Mathematics, Statistics, or a related field by the time of appointment. While the doctoral degree is the standard requirement, individuals holding a Master of Arts (MA) or Master of Science (MS) in Mathematics or Statistics will be considered if they demonstrate a record of exceptional teaching and professional experience. Successful applicants will demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and have the ability to effectively instruct a diverse range of courses. Beyond academic credentials, the ideal candidates will also possess strong communication and interpersonal skills, a proven track record of engaging with a diverse student body, and experience in curriculum support or student success initiatives. Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, applications should be submitted online at https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37798 by June 12, 2026. Applications should include a cover letter outlining your teaching interests and relevant experience, current curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, copies of graduate transcripts. In addition, names and contact information for three letters of recommendation must be provided. The application system will contact the letter writers via email and provide them with instructions for uploading their letters. The search will remain open until the position is filled. School/College & Department/Program Summary The Department of Mathematics and Statistics at Oakland University provides students opportunities to develop the analytical and problem-solving skills needed for a vast array of modern careers. As one of the largest departments in the College of Arts and Sciences, we offer a broad range of undergraduate and graduate programs, including Bachelor’s degrees in Mathematics, Mathematics for Educators, Applied Statistics, Actuarial Science, and Applied Data Science as well as Master’s and Ph.D. programs in applied mathematical sciences. Our department serves a vital support role across the university, providing essential quantitative training for other schools, including School of Engineering and Computer Science, the School of Business Administration, and the School of Education and Human Services. We are a community of active scholars and dedicated educators committed to providing a dynamic learning environment, ranging from foundational lower-level courses to cutting-edge research opportunities. More About Oakland University The University is located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University offers 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan that is dedicated to building ongoing, collaborative relationships, Oakland University embraces community and civic engagement to enhance the lives of its students and positively impact the broader community. Learn more about Oakland University’s Mission & Vision and Strategic Plan . Pay Basis Open Date 05/26/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Job Category Visiting Faculty EEO Statement Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/39143": {
      "title": "Special Instructor in Chemistry",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Special Instructor in Chemistry Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Special Instructor in Chemistry Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For full consideration, applications should be submitted online at https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37631 by June 8, 2026. Applications should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching statement including teaching philosophy, examples of recent course syllabi, and unofficial transcripts. In addition, names and contact information for three letters of recommendation must be provided. The application system will contact the letter writers via email and provide them with instructions for uploading their letters. Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. Inquiries should be addressed to: Dr. Jennifer Tillinger, Department of Chemistry ( jbulgare@oakland.edu ). Posting Details Position Information Job Title Special Instructor in Chemistry Department 0542 - Chemistry Requisition No. 0000822 Job Description Summary The Department of Chemistry at Oakland University invites applications for a full-time faculty position in chemistry, with an anticipated start date of August 15, 2026. The appointment at the rank of Special Instructor is a full-time, teaching-focused faculty position that leads to job security equivalent to tenure. Special Instructors are expected to teach three courses (or the equivalent) during both the Fall and Winter semesters and to contribute to departmental service. The department offers courses that support a wide range of majors and programs, including Chemistry, Biology, Health Sciences, Biomedical Sciences, and Engineering. The successful candidate will be expected to teach introductory/foundational lecture and laboratory courses within the chemistry curriculum. Potential teaching assignments include general chemistry, analytical chemistry, and related chemistry courses aligned with departmental needs and the candidate’s expertise. Opportunities for additional compensation may be available through summer teaching assignments during the May–August term. Minimum Qualifications Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in chemistry, or a related field, and have experience in teaching both lecture and laboratory courses in general chemistry. Candidates that have demonstrated experience in course development, teaching courses at multiple levels, and designing courses in different modalities (e.g., online vs. in person) will be given favorable consideration. Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, applications should be submitted online at https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37631 by June 8, 2026. Applications should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching statement including teaching philosophy, examples of recent course syllabi, and unofficial transcripts. In addition, names and contact information for three letters of recommendation must be provided. The application system will contact the letter writers via email and provide them with instructions for uploading their letters. Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. Inquiries should be addressed to: Dr. Jennifer Tillinger, Department of Chemistry ( jbulgare@oakland.edu ). School/College & Department/Program Summary The Department of Chemistry ( https://wwwp.oakland.edu/chemistry/ ) is a research-oriented department with Master’s and Ph.D. programs. More About Oakland University The University is located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University offers 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan that is dedicated to building ongoing, collaborative relationships, Oakland University embraces community and civic engagement to enhance the lives of its students and positively impact the broader community. Learn more about Oakland University’s Mission & Vision and Strategic Plan . Pay Basis Open Date 05/18/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Job Category Full-time Faculty EEO Statement Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Teaching Statement Sample Syllabus Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/39123": {
      "title": "Part-Time Clinical, Lab, or Simulation Faculty - School of Nursing",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Part-Time Clinical, Lab, or Simulation Faculty - School of Nursing Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Part-Time Clinical, Lab, or Simulation Faculty - School of Nursing Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Contact information for references will be requested. In your cover letter, please specify the roles, specialties, or programs that you wish to teach. Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Nursing Department: 0090 - Nursing Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Nursing Name of Department Chair: Lori Davidson, Maria Vitale Expected Hire Date: 01/04/2027 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Part-Time Clinical, Lab, or Simulation Faculty - School of Nursing Job Description Summary: Part-Time Faculty provide direct instruction and supervision of students in the BSN or MSN programs. They possess a significant knowledge base in their specialty area (Pediatrics, Psych/Mental Health, Obstetrics – Mother/Baby, Medical/Surgical, and/or Community Health) and bring a wealth of experience, as well as awareness of current practice issues and trends. Complete all related teaching responsibilities such as enforcing attendance policies, teaching students to apply what they are learning in class in the clinical environment, evaluating student clinical performance, completing clinical site evaluations, etc. Participate in routine meetings with the Faculty of Record ( FOR ) to review the syllabus and course expectations. Manage clinical, lab, or simulation instructional settings and environments through active instructor presence to promote a positive learning atmosphere. Fulfill professional responsibilities by following all SON policies and procedures, attending SON and course orientation, meeting with the course faculty of record as needed, and completing clinical site orientation requirements when necessary. Academically coach, guide, mentor, monitor progress, and empower students to achieve optimum success. Provide students with academic support and offer referrals for additional assistance as required, tutor if necessary, and provide other assistance as needed. We interview and hire throughout the academic year. The expected hire date is based on the first date you would be working in the clinical or lab setting and this date will vary. Minimum Qualifications: Graduate degree in nursing or related/relevant field required. Minimum of three (3) years of recent RN experience required. Previous experience as a clinical instructor preferred. Current, active, unrestricted license as a registered nurse (RN) in the State of Michigan required. Clean criminal background check and urine drug screen required. Must be able to meet all health requirements and training requirements as stipulated by the clinical agencies. Special Instructions to Applicants: Contact information for references will be requested. In your cover letter, please specify the roles, specialties, or programs that you wish to teach. Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 09/23/2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) List of References Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
