      "title": "Athletics Broadcast Assistant",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Athletics Broadcast Assistant Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Athletics Broadcast Assistant Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Athletics Broadcast Assistant Department 2836 - Athletics Administration Position Number E44286 Requisition No. TC06428 Salary Range/Pay Rate 25.00 per hour Benefits of Working at Oakland University No benefits are associated with this position. Employee Group/Grade Casual Job Category Casual /Temporary Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule Casual (19hrs or less, No Benefits ) Shift/Days Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. 19 Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 06/15/2026 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. n/a Minimum Qualifications Technical Proficiency: At least 1-2 years of experience in live sports production, broadcast journalism, or a related technical field (e.g., AV setup, live streaming). Specialized Skillset: Proven ability to perform in the following key area: Production: Operation of professional-grade broadcast cameras (e.g., Sony, Panasonic) and knowledge of signal flow ( SDI , HDMI , XLR ). Physical Requirements: Ability to lift and carry up to 50 lbs. of broadcast equipment and stand for the duration of a standard athletic event (approx. 3–5 hours). Schedule Reliability: Must have a flexible schedule with the ability to work consistent nights, weekends, and occasional holidays in alignment with the [Athletics Department] game schedule. Professional Communication: Demonstrated ability to take rapid-fire direction via an intercom headset ( IFB ) in a high-pressure, live-event environment. Desired Qualifications ESPN+ Standards: Previous experience working on productions that meet ESPN+ or similar Division I digital/linear broadcast standards. System Knowledge: Experience with specific production hardware/software such as: NewTek Tricaster or Ross Video switchers. ScoreVision or similar jumbotron/in-game entertainment software. DVSport or similar instant replay systems. Athletic Knowledge: Strong working knowledge of NCAA rules and game-flow for multiple sports (specifically Basketball, Soccer, Volleyball, Baseball/Softball). Local Proximity: Resides within a 50-mile radius of Rochester, MI, to accommodate short-notice “break-fix” or “fill-in” opportunities. Position Purpose To provide a specialized and technical skillset for our live sports productions. Job Duties Provide a specialized and technical skillset for our live sports productions. Job Open Date 06/10/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
