    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/39104": {
      "title": "Communications Manager, Office of the Provost",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Communications Manager, Office of the Provost Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Communications Manager, Office of the Provost Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Communications Manager, Office of the Provost Department 7159 - Communications & Marketing Position Number 986394 Requisition No. S02806 Salary Range/Pay Rate $60,000 annually Benefits of Working at Oakland University Oakland University offers competitive salaries and an excellent benefit program including a comprehensive medical plan with low contribution amounts for our employees, dental and vision plans at no cost for our employees, generous paid time off plans, a generous University contribution to our 403(b) retirement plan, tuition assistance for our employees and dependents, free access to our Campus Recreation Center and workout facilities, and flexible work schedules and wellness programs. These are current benefit levels subject to future changes. Employee Group/Grade AP Band N Job Category Administrative-Professional Work Schedule FT/Reg (40 hours) Shift/Days This is a full-time position. First consideration will be given to those who apply by August 20, 2026. Pay Schedule Month Number of Hrs./Wk. 40 Position Information Position Information Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in communications, journalism, marketing, English, public relations, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and/or experience. A minimum of two (2) years of progressively responsible experience in communications, marketing, or a related field, with demonstrated strength in writing, digital channel management, and project coordination. Excellent written communication skills across multiple formats and audiences, including institutional messaging, social media, newsletters, and executive correspondence. Demonstrated ability to work independently, manage competing priorities, and exercise sound judgment with minimal day-to-day supervision. Experience managing organizational social media accounts, including content planning, scheduling, community monitoring, and analytics. Experience using content management systems to edit and maintain websites. Strong organizational and project management skills; ability to meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment with multiple concurrent priorities. Professional maturity and interpersonal skills appropriate to a senior leadership environment; ability to handle sensitive and confidential information with discretion. Desired Qualifications Master’s degree in communications, marketing, higher education, or a related field. Experience working in a higher education or complex institutional setting. Experience supporting executive-level communications, including writing in an established institutional or individual voice. Familiarity with brand governance principles and experience working within an institutional brand framework. Experience with email marketing platforms and web analytics tools. Knowledge of and enthusiasm for the academic mission of a regional public university. All Qualifications Unless otherwise required by an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Position Details Position Purpose The Communications Manager serves as the primary communications resource for Academic Affairs—owning the day-to-day execution of the Provost’s communications plan while also bringing strategic judgment and independent initiative to the role. This is a standalone embedded position. The Communications Manager operates with a high degree of autonomy, managing the full scope of Academic Affairs communications: executive content for the Provost, internal communications across schools and colleges, digital channel management, brand stewardship, and coordination with UCM’s central teams. The Manager is the sole dedicated communications professional for one of the university’s most complex and high-visibility leadership offices, and will act as a trusted liaison, ensuring all communications are handled with confidentiality and professional discretion. The ideal candidate brings both strong execution skills and the professional maturity to work independently in a senior leadership environment, advise the Provost on communications decisions, and serve as a credible representative of UCM’s standards across the Academic Affairs community. Job Open Date 08/07/2026 Job Close Date Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a member of the Oakland University Administrative-Professional Group? Yes No No Response Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
