      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Assistant General Counsel Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Assistant General Counsel Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Assistant General Counsel Department 4112 - Legal Affairs/Gen Counsel/Bd Of Trustees Position Number 986386 Requisition No. S02817 Salary Range/Pay Rate Salary commensurate with education and experience. Benefits of Working at Oakland University Oakland University offers competitive salaries and an excellent benefit program including a comprehensive medical plan with low contribution amounts for our employees, dental and vision plans at no cost for our employees, generous paid time off plans, a generous University contribution to our 403(b) retirement plan, tuition assistance for our employees and dependents, free access to our Campus Recreation Center and workout facilities, and flexible work schedules and wellness programs. These are current benefit levels subject to future changes. Employee Group/Grade AP Band W Job Category Administrative-Professional Work Schedule FT/Reg (40 hours) Shift/Days This is a full-time position. First consideration will be given to those who apply by August 26, 2026. Pay Schedule Month Number of Hrs./Wk. 40 Position Information Position Information Minimum Qualifications J. D. degree from an accredited law school. License to practice law in the State of Michigan or immediate eligibility for admission. A minimum of three (3) years of progressively responsible experience in a broad range of relevant legal areas. Excellent interpersonal, analytical, conflict resolution, and written and oral communication skills; and collegial disposition. Desired Qualifications Familiarity with higher education or public sector law. FOIA experience. EEOC , MDCR OCR and other agency experience. Significant litigation experience. Experience in the practice areas described in the Position Purpose statement below. Preference for applicants with significant prior experience in labor (e.g., collective bargaining, grievances, arbitrations, etc.) and employment law. All Qualifications Unless otherwise required by an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Position Details Position Purpose Assist the General Counsel in providing legal services to the University on an extensive range of legal matters including without limitation general business, board governance, constitutional law, compliance, governmental immunity, intellectual property, patent, copyright, health care, labor and employment, employee benefits, tax, contracts, academic and policy issues, real estate and construction, bankruptcy, charter schools, immigration, privacy and data security, software agreements, planned giving, gifts, endowments, government regulations, charitable gaming, FOIA , HIPAA , COBRA , FERPA , Clery Act, FMLA , litigation, scientific research, police/criminal law, risk management, liquor license and other assigned areas and duties consistent with the skills, interests and needs of the office. Job Open Date 08/13/2026 Job Close Date Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a member of the Oakland University Administrative-Professional Group? Yes No No Response * Describe your prior work experience in any of the specific practice areas described in the Position Purpose statement of the Position Description. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience with online forms such as Google Docs, eforms, etc and with virtual platforms such as Google Meet, Zoom, etc. (Open Ended Question) * Are you willing to work non-traditional work hours such as nights and weekends and to schedule time off around large scale university events? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Writing Sample Publication 1 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
