    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/39063": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Counseling",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Lecturer in Counseling Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Lecturer in Counseling Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach any relevant certifications and/or licenses. Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Education & Human Services Department: 1770 - Counseling Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Counseling Name of Department Chair: Jennifer Matthews Expected Hire Date: 09/01/2026 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Lecturer in Counseling Job Description Summary: The Department of Counseling at Oakland University, Rochester, Michigan is seeking applicants for part-time Lecturers to teach courses in their MA and Ph.D. CACREP -accredited programs. Preferred qualifications include a) a doctorate or ABD in Counselor Education/Counseling or closely related field; b) a minimum of 3 years of clinical experience in school or clinical mental health counseling; c) graduate-level teaching experience; d) the ability to deliver courses in-class and online. The review of applications is ongoing and continuous. Position availability varies by semester, depending on the needs of the department. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in a relevant discipline, preferably counseling, but psychology and social work may be considered Competence in working with students from diverse populations and backgrounds Willingness to use a web-based learning management system Familiarity with navigating video conferencing platforms (such as Zoom) with the intent to use in some classroom or other interpersonal settings Special Instructions to Applicants: Please attach any relevant certifications and/or licenses. Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. Open Date: 09/16/2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Transcripts (unofficial) Optional Documents Licenses/Certifications 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
