    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38860": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science - American Politics",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Political Science - American Politics Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Assistant Professor of Political Science - American Politics Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, writing sample, unofficial graduate transcripts, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and contact information for at least three references through Oakland University’s online application system. Once all required application materials have been uploaded through the online system, references will be contacted through the online system to submit confidential letters of recommendation. Applicants may also submit teaching evaluations, a writing sample, and a research statement. Review of applications will begin on October 12, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Questions regarding the position should be directed to Dr. Terri L. Towner, American Politics Search Chair, at towner@oakland.edu. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of Political Science - American Politics Department 1346 - Political Science Requisition No. 0000839 Job Description Summary The Department of Political Science at Oakland University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position in American Politics at the rank of Assistant Professor, beginning August 15, 2027. We seek a candidate broadly trained in American Politics with an active research agenda and a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching. The area of specialization within American Politics is open. The successful candidate will be expected to teach an introductory course in American politics and upper-division courses in political behavior and/or political institutions (other than the judiciary), as well as courses in the candidate’s areas of expertise. The ability to contribute to the department’s research methods sequence is highly desirable. Oakland University operates on the semester system, and the standard teaching load is five courses per academic year. Minimum Qualifications Candidates with their Ph.D. in hand are preferred, but candidates who are ABD will also be considered, provided that they can demonstrate they are near completion of the dissertation. Candidates should demonstrate the potential for a productive scholarly research program, excellence in undergraduate teaching, and a commitment to advising and mentoring undergraduate research. Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, writing sample, unofficial graduate transcripts, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and contact information for at least three references through Oakland University’s online application system. Once all required application materials have been uploaded through the online system, references will be contacted through the online system to submit confidential letters of recommendation. Applicants may also submit teaching evaluations, a writing sample, and a research statement. Review of applications will begin on October 12, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Questions regarding the position should be directed to Dr. Terri L. Towner, American Politics Search Chair, at towner@oakland.edu. School/College & Department/Program Summary The Department of Political Science, housed in the College of Arts and Sciences, offers undergraduate degree programs in Political Science (B.A.), International Relations (B.A.), and Public Administration and Public Policy (B.S.), as well as a NASPAA -accredited Master of Public Administration (M.P.A.) program. The Department also conducts applied research for public and nonprofit agencies through the Public Affairs Research Laboratory. More About Oakland University The University is located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University offers 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan that is dedicated to building ongoing, collaborative relationships, Oakland University embraces community and civic engagement to enhance the lives of its students and positively impact the broader community. Learn more about Oakland University’s Mission & Vision and Strategic Plan . Pay Basis Open Date 08/26/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Job Category Full-time Faculty EEO Statement Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Teaching Statement Writing Sample Optional Documents Teaching Evaluation Research Statement Writing Sample (2) 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38726": {
      "title": "GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position: Clare-Gladwin Counties",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position: Clare-Gladwin Counties Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position: Clare-Gladwin Counties Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position: Clare-Gladwin Counties Department 2055 - Human Development & Child Study Position Number E36678 Requisition No. TC06465 Salary Range/Pay Rate $26 per hour Benefits of Working at Oakland University No benefits are associated with this position. Employee Group/Grade Casual Job Category Casual Posted Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule Casual (19hrs or less, No Benefits ) Shift/Days We are seeking applicants available for 2–3 weekday mornings during preschool classroom hours in September–October and April–May to conduct in-person child assessments. Some afternoon and/or evening availability will also be needed to complete required post-assessment paperwork. Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. 5-7 Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 08/24/2026 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. 08/30/2027 Minimum Qualifications Experience working with preschool children Available to work week-day morning hours Must have reliable transportation Ability to follow specific, standardized protocols Strong organizational skills Excellent interpersonal, oral and written communication skills Willingness to learn new technology Desired Qualifications Familiarity with Michigan’s state-funded Prekindergarten program, Great Start Readiness Program ( GSRP ), and Michigan’s early childhood landscape Prior experience conducting child assessments in early childhood classrooms Position Purpose The Department of Human Development and Child Studies ( HDCS ), housed in the School of Education and Human Services, invites applications for several part-time Data Collector positions to work on a statewide preschool evaluation. We are seeking applicants available for 2–3 weekday mornings during preschool classroom hours in September–October and April–May to conduct in-person child assessments. Some afternoon and/or evening availability will also be needed to complete required post-assessment paperwork. Job Duties Responsibilities include completing a mandatory training to be held in late August (date TBD ), contacting teachers to arrange – mutually-agreed upon times to assess study children in their classrooms, driving to sites in the counties of Clare and Gladwin, and additional tasks as assigned. Must pass a background check prior to hiring/starting. Job Open Date 08/14/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter List of References Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
