    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38605": {
      "title": "Athletics Game Day Stats Assistant",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Athletics Game Day Stats Assistant Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Athletics Game Day Stats Assistant Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Athletics Game Day Stats Assistant Department 2836 - Athletics Administration Position Number E42912 Requisition No. TC06473 Salary Range/Pay Rate 15.00 hr Benefits of Working at Oakland University No benefits are associated with this position. Employee Group/Grade Casual Job Category Casual /Temporary Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule Casual (19hrs or less, No Benefits ) Shift/Days Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. 19 Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 09/01/2026 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. n/a Minimum Qualifications High School diploma or an equivalent combination of education and experience Ability to learn LiveStats through NCAA Genius for multiple sports. There is opportunity to be trained Experience working in high-pressure live event environments with real-time direction Ability to remain focused, professional, and neutral in team support for 3–5-hour events. Strong communication skills and ability to respond quickly to in-game changes Flexible schedule including evenings, weekends, and occasional holidays Ability to work consistently with athletic event schedules and last-minute changes Strong attention to detail and accuracy under pressure Professional, reliable, and team-oriented approach in live event settings Resides within a 50-mile radius of Rochester, MI, to accommodate short-notice opportunities. Ability to follow NCAA , Conference, and University rules, regulations, guidelines, policies and procedures Desired Qualifications Previous experience working stats with NCAA Livestats through Genius Familiarity with collegiate athletics and game flow for sports such as basketball, soccer, volleyball, baseball, and softball Experience working within Division I athletics or similar high-level sports environments Strong understanding of NCAA game structure and in-game timing Experience working with live production teams and in-arena entertainment environments Position Purpose The Gameday Stats Assistant serves as the official stats taker at live home athletic events to be distributed to GoldenGrizzlies.com, ESPN , NCAA , and other media entities. This role is responsible for taking/inputting accurate stats into the NCAA Livestats Genius software based on the live action in-game. Job Duties Assist in game set-up and tear-down of stat techology/computers on gameday Input or call stats on Genius program accurately and efficiently Print and/or deliver stat boxscores as needed Take direction quickly from SID and game operations staff Maintain professionalism throughout game to show neutrality and unbiased stat taking Job Open Date 08/06/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38584": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Education",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Education Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Assistant Professor of Education Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Required documents for the application include: Curriculum vitae (CV) Cover letter Teaching statement Research statement One representative publication Names of and contact information for three (and up to five) references Optional documents: Up to three representative publications Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of Education Department 2055 - Human Development & Child Study Requisition No. 0000829 Job Description Summary The Department of Human Development and Child Studies ( HDCS ) at Oakland University invites applications for a tenure-track, benefits-eligible faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin in August 15, 2027 . The successful candidate will join the Special Education area and contribute primarily to the Applied Behavior Analysis ( ABA ) graduate program. Responsibilities include teaching graduate coursework in ABA , mentoring graduate students, maintaining an active scholarly agenda, and contributing to departmental, school, university, and professional service activities. The standard teaching load is 3 courses in one semester and 2 courses in the other semester. Teaching responsibilities will include mentorship and supervision of graduate students enrolled in the program’s Experiential Learning/Exit Project sequence and may include courses such as Experimental Analysis of Behavior, Behavior Change Procedures, and other graduate-level ABA courses consistent with the candidate’s expertise and program needs. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued growth and quality of the ABA program, including support of ABAI Recognition and future accreditation efforts. Candidates with interests that complement existing faculty expertise and who demonstrate potential for future leadership within the program are especially encouraged to apply. Review of applications will begin September 7 and continue until the position is filled. For further information, please contact the Chair of the Search Committee: Dr. Michael Kranak kranak@oakland.edu Minimum Qualifications Required/Minimum Qualifications: Terminal degree (Ph.D., Ed.D., or Psy.D.) in applied behavior analysis, behavior analysis, or a closely related field (e.g., psychology, special education, school psychology). Candidates who are ABD (all but dissertation) with expected degree completion by August 15, 2027 may be considered. Board Certified Behavior Analyst ( BCBA ) in good standing, eligible for licensure in Michigan, and eligible to supervise trainees accruing supervised fieldwork (i.e., completion of the 8-hr BACB supervision training). Ability to mentor and supervise graduate students engaged in scholarly, clinical, and experiential learning activities; and a demonstrated commitment to the science-based practice of behavior analysis and evidence-based, data-based decision making. Evidence of scholarly productivity or strong potential for an active research agenda that complements those of existing faculty. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal, and organizational communication skills. Desired/Preferred Qualifications: Record of peer-reviewed scholarly publications. Potential for obtaining extramural funding through grants and contracts. Evidence of successful teaching in face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online learning environments, or strong potential for excellence in teaching. Experience teaching graduate-level courses in behavior analysis. Experience supervising student research, capstone projects, theses/thesis-like activities, dissertations, or comparable scholarly activities. Experience providing behavior-analytic services across educational, clinical, community, vocational, employment, or post-secondary settings. Commitment to (or experience in) contributing to ABAI Recognition, accreditation, assessment, and continuous program improvement efforts. Special Instructions to Applicants Required documents for the application include: Curriculum vitae (CV) Cover letter Teaching statement Research statement One representative publication Names of and contact information for three (and up to five) references Optional documents: Up to three representative publications School/College & Department/Program Summary HDCS includes Special Education and Early Childhood programs. The programs in the Special Education area include: ABA , Emotional Impairment, Specific Learning Disability, and Autism Spectrum Disorder. HDCS currently has nine faculty members, five of whom are primarily assigned to Special Education. More About Oakland University The University is located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University offers 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan that is dedicated to building ongoing, collaborative relationships, Oakland University embraces community and civic engagement to enhance the lives of its students and positively impact the broader community. Learn more about Oakland University’s Mission & Vision and Strategic Plan . Pay Basis Open Date 08/05/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Job Category Full-time Faculty EEO Statement Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Teaching Statement Research Statement Publication 1 Optional Documents Publication 2 Publication 3 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
