    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38515": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Special Lecturer – Human Movement Science",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Lecturer/Special Lecturer – Human Movement Science Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Lecturer/Special Lecturer – Human Movement Science Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Health Sciences Department: 0738 - Human Movement Science Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Physical Therapy Name of Department Chair: John Krauss Expected Hire Date: 09/01/2026 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Lecturer/Special Lecturer – Human Movement Science Job Description Summary: Oakland University is searching for a Lecturer/Instructor of Record to teach physical therapy courses for the department of human movement science students. The lecturer will be required to develop and deliver the assigned course based on the syllabus, address and assess the student learning outcomes stated in the syllabus, and issue timely course grades. This will be in collaboration with the program director and relevant program faculty to ensure compliance with accreditation competency requirements. The instructor of record will be responsible for adhering to the general terms outlined for lecturers and for following the University guidelines for instruction and grading as stated in the university catalog. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s or Doctoral degree in physical therapy, health professional field, medical field or related field of expertise Special Instructions to Applicants: Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 07/27/2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) List of References Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
