      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Lecturer - Clinical and Diagnostic Sciences Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Lecturer - Clinical and Diagnostic Sciences Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Health Sciences Department: 0729 - Clinical and Diagnostic Sciences Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Clinical and Diagnostic Sciences Name of Department Chair: Sumit Dinda Expected Hire Date: 09/01/2026 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Lecturer - Clinical and Diagnostic Sciences Job Description Summary: Oakland University is searching for an instructor to assist in teaching for the department of Clinical and Diagnostic Sciences. The individual is required to assist in delivering the assigned courses based on the syllabus, address the student learning outcomes stated in the syllabus, and issue timely course grades. The individual will be responsible for adhering to the general terms outlined for lecturers and for following the University guidelines for instruction and grading as stated in the university catalog. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in a related health science field. Minimum three years healthcare work experience preferred. College teaching experience is preferred but not required. Special Instructions to Applicants: Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 07/16/2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) List of References Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
