    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37757": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Post Doctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Post Doctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Education & Human Services Department: 2055 - Human Development & Child Study Position Title: Other Field of Specialty: Early Childhood Name of Department Chair: Tomoko Wakabayashi Expected Hire Date: 08/15/2026 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Post Doctoral Research Associate Job Description Summary: The Department of Human Development and Child Studies ( HDCS ), housed in the School of Education and Human Services, invites applications to a full-time Postdoctoral Research Associate position to work on a newly funded statewide preschool evaluation. Postdoctoral Research Associate will be expected to work closely with the PI, Co-PI and the Project manager to conduct advanced statistical analysis and data visualization. This person will also help with report writing; peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations, and additional tasks as assigned. The position is grant-funded, contingent upon continued funding, and begins August 15, 2026. Possibility for renewal up to 3 years, pending performance and fund availability. Please submit your CV, cover letter, 3 references, copy of your post-secondary transcripts (unofficial is acceptable), and two writing samples for consideration. Minimum Qualifications: Strong interest and knowledge of Michigan’s early childhood landscape PhD in Early Childhood Education, Human Development, or related field received in the past 5 years (2021-2026). ABD will be considered on a limited basis. Advanced knowledge in statistical analysis ( SPSS . STATA or R). Demonstrated background in Python programming, statistical modeling, and data visualization (Tableau or Power BI). Experience working in a collaborative team environment Excellent interpersonal, oral and written communication skills Good command of Google Suite Open to learning new technology and research approaches Special Instructions to Applicants: Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 05/18/2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Writing Sample Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
