    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37531": {
      "title": "Clinical Laboratory Assistants",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Clinical Laboratory Assistants Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Clinical Laboratory Assistants Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. We interview and hire throughout the academic year. The expected hire date is based on the first date you would be working in the laboratory setting, and this date will vary. Appointment will be part-time, with effort defined by assigned instructional responsibilities. Responsibilities may include daytime, evening, or occasional weekend activities. Clinical Laboratory Assistants do not hold administrative or program leadership responsibilities unless separately appointed. Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Health Sciences Department: 0729 - Clinical and Diagnostic Sciences Position Title: Other Field of Specialty: Physician Assistant Science Name of Department Chair: Sumit Dinda Expected Hire Date: 09/01/2026 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Clinical Laboratory Assistants Job Description Summary: The Clinical Laboratory Assistant for the Physician Assistant (PA) Program supports the delivery of clinical skills and patient assessment education by preparing, maintaining, and assisting with laboratory and simulation activities. This role ensures that instructional sessions run efficiently and students have a safe, organized, and effective environment to develop clinical competencies aligned with program learning outcomes and accreditation standards. Laboratory Assistants work collaboratively with Program leadership and colleagues to support curriculum delivery while adhering to institutional policies and accreditation requirements. Job Description Summary Prepare clinical skills laboratories for instructional sessions, including physical exam, procedural skills, and patient assessment activities. Set up and break down equipment, supplies, and simulation stations before and after sessions. Assist faculty during skills labs, OSCEs, and simulation exercises. Support standardized patient encounters and simulation-based learning activities. Help coordinate student flow and timing during OSCEs and practical exams. Assist in troubleshooting minor issues during lab sessions. Assess student performance fairly and consistently using established rubrics and evaluation criteria, and deliver timely, constructive feedback that promotes learning and professional growth. Maintain confidentiality and professionalism during student assessments. Serve as a role model for professional behavior, ethical practice, and interprofessional collaboration. Support remediation activities when assigned, in collaboration with Course Directors and Program leadership. Maintain current clinical knowledge and professional competence in assigned instructional areas. Adhere to institutional policies, Program policies, and accreditation standards. Minimum Qualifications: Graduate degree from an accredited Physician Assistant program. Minimum of 2 years of clinical experience as a PA. Eligibility for licensure or current licensure as a Physician Assistant in the state of employment Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and work collaboratively in an academic environment. Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching experience in PA, medical, or allied health education. Experience with laboratory instruction, simulation, or clinical skills teaching. Familiarity with competency-based education, assessment strategies, and educational technology. Special Instructions to Applicants: We interview and hire throughout the academic year. The expected hire date is based on the first date you would be working in the laboratory setting, and this date will vary. Appointment will be part-time, with effort defined by assigned instructional responsibilities. Responsibilities may include daytime, evening, or occasional weekend activities. Clinical Laboratory Assistants do not hold administrative or program leadership responsibilities unless separately appointed. Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 04/27/2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
