    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37491": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Special Lecturer of Chinese Language and Culture",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Lecturer/Special Lecturer of Chinese Language and Culture Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Lecturer/Special Lecturer of Chinese Language and Culture Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, upload a cover letter addressing teaching philosophy and qualifications, current curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts and contact information for two (2) professional references. Position Approval Information First Section School/College: College of Arts & Sciences Department: 1107 - Modern Languages & Literatures Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Chinese Name of Department Chair: Adolfo Campoy-Cubillo Expected Hire Date: 08/15/2026 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Lecturer/Special Lecturer of Chinese Language and Culture Job Description Summary: The Department of Modern Languages and Literatures invites applications for the position of Lecturer of Chinese Language and Culture . We seek a dynamic and committed educator to teach undergraduate in Chinese language (elementary through advanced levels) and Chinese culture , including literature, film, history, and contemporary issues. The ideal candidate will have a passion for student-centered teaching and demonstrate a commitment to inclusive and intercultural pedagogies. Key Responsibilities: Teach at least one Chinese language and/or culture course per semester. Develop syllabi, lesson plans, and assessments aligned with departmental learning goals. Use communicative and immersive methods to promote language proficiency and cultural literacy. Foster an inclusive classroom environment that supports diverse learners. Integrate authentic materials (films, music, news media, literature) to enhance cultural understanding. Participate in curriculum development and contribute to departmental initiatives. Support student engagement through cultural events, language tables, study abroad advising, etc. Minimum Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree or higher in Chinese Linguistics, Chinese Literature, Language Education, or a closely related field. Native or near-native proficiency in Chinese and English. Demonstrated experience teaching Chinese at the university or secondary level. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching both language and content courses (e.g., calligraphy, cinema, cultural studies). Familiarity with ACTFL standards, proficiency-based instruction, and digital language learning tools. Evidence of inclusive pedagogy and commitment to equity in the classroom. Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply, upload a cover letter addressing teaching philosophy and qualifications, current curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts and contact information for two (2) professional references. Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 04/23/2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) List of References Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
