    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37298": {
      "title": "Environmental Health and Safety Lecturer",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Environmental Health and Safety Lecturer Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Environmental Health and Safety Lecturer Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, upload a cover letter addressing relevant experience, evidence of a commitment to student success, current vita, and an unofficial transcript. For questions or to inquire about opportunities, please contact Dr. Tara Diesbourg at tdiesbourg@oakland.edu. Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Health Sciences Department: 1034 - Public and Environment Wellness Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Environmental Health and Safety Name of Department Chair: Flora Dallo Expected Hire Date: 08/17/2026 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Environmental Health and Safety Lecturer Job Description Summary: Oakland University is seeking a passionate and dedicated instructor to teach a senior-level ergonomics course to students in the Environmental Health and Safety ( EHS ) and Master of Science in Safety Management ( MSSM ) programs. The course focuses on Ergonomics and related change management concepts, anthropometry, biomechanics, metabolic energy expenditure, capabilities and limitations of workers; design and analysis of the workplace, hand tools, controls and products; applications of the NIOSH lifting guidelines and other standards. The ideal candidate will have expertise in biomechanics and/or ergonomics, with experience practicing ergonomics in industrial settings. Responsibilities: · Develop and teach a course on ergonomics that covers everything from functional anatomy and anthropometry, to ergonomics risk factors, to assessment and risk mitigation. · Engage students in completing actual ergonomics assessments and getting hand-on experience in practicing ergonomics in their communities. · Maintain student engagement and active participation in a fully-online course environment · Foster a supportive and inclusive learning environment that promotes student success · Address and assess the student learning outcomes stated in the syllabus, and issue timely course grades · Remain available for student meetings and inquiry, hosting online office hours and tutorials as needed · Adhere to the general terms outlined for lecturers and follow the University guidelines for instruction and grading as stated in the university catalog Minimum Qualifications: Master’s or Doctoral degree in Biomechanics, Ergonomics, or Environmental Health and Safety (with ergonomics specialty credentials/certificates). Preference will be given to applicants with a proven track record of teaching high quality, online courses. Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply, upload a cover letter addressing relevant experience, evidence of a commitment to student success, current vita, and an unofficial transcript. For questions or to inquire about opportunities, please contact Dr. Tara Diesbourg at tdiesbourg@oakland.edu. Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 03/27/2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) List of References Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
