    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37076": {
      "title": "Oakland GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Oakland GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Oakland GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Oakland GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position Department 2055 - Human Development & Child Study Position Number X36678 Requisition No. TC06214 Salary Range/Pay Rate $26 per hour Benefits of Working at Oakland University No benefits are associated with this position. Employee Group/Grade Temporary Job Category Casual /Temporary Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule PT/Temp (20-39 hours, No Benefits ) Shift/Days Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. 20-30 Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 04/01/2026 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. 05/31/2026 Minimum Qualifications Experience working with preschool children Available to work week-day morning hours Must have reliable transportation Ability to follow specific, standardized protocols Strong organizational skills Excellent interpersonal, oral and written communication skills Willingness to learn new technology Valid driver’s license & a driving record acceptable to the University’s insurance carrier. Desired Qualifications Familiarity with Michigan’s state-funded Prekindergarten program, Great Start Readiness Program ( GSRP ), and Michigan’s early childhood landscape Prior experience conducting child assessments in early childhood classrooms Position Purpose The Department of Human Development and Child Studies ( HDCS ), housed in the School of Education and Human Services, invites applications for several part-time Data Collector positions to work on a newly funded statewide preschool evaluation. The Data Collectors will be required to work a total of 20-30 flexible weekday hours between the months of April – May (total across both months) to conduct in-person child assessments. Prior to hire, the Oakland GSRP Evaluation Data Collector must complete criminal background screening, drug screening, the State of Michigan Licensing Background check and fingerprinting, and a TB test with physician’s signature. Job Duties Responsibilities include completing a mandatory training to be held in early April (date TBD ), contacting teachers to arrange a mutually-agreed upon time to assess study children in their classrooms, driving to sites in the Oakland County area, and additional tasks as assigned. Job Open Date 03/02/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
