    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/36949": {
      "title": "Part-Time Instructional Faculty - Physician Assistant Program",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Part-Time Instructional Faculty - Physician Assistant Program Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Part-Time Instructional Faculty - Physician Assistant Program Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Health Sciences Department: 0729 - Clinical and Diagnostic Sciences Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Physician Assistant Science Name of Department Chair: Sumit Dinda Expected Hire Date: 05/01/2026 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Part-Time Instructional Faculty - Physician Assistant Program Job Description Summary: Instructional Faculty in the Physician Assistant Program are responsible for delivering high-quality didactic, laboratory, and/or clinical skills instruction that supports the Program’s mission, learning outcomes, and accreditation standards. Faculty in this role contribute clinical expertise, evidence-based teaching, and learner-centered instruction to prepare PA students for competent, ethical, and patient-centered practice. Instructional Faculty work collaboratively with Program leadership and faculty to support curriculum delivery while adhering to institutional policies and accreditation requirements. Minimum Qualifications: Graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant program. Current NCCPA certification (PA-C). Eligibility for licensure or current licensure as a Physician Assistant in the state of Michigan. Minimum of 3 years of relevant clinical experience in the instructional content area. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and work collaboratively in an academic environment. Ability to stand for extended periods during laboratory or skills-based instruction. Use of personal protective equipment ( PPE ) as required. Ability to demonstrate clinical skills and procedures. Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching experience in PA, medical, or allied health education. Experience with lecturing or clinical skills teaching. Familiarity with competency-based education, assessment strategies, and educational technology. Special Instructions to Applicants: Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 02/16/2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Licenses/Certifications Transcripts (unofficial) Optional Documents Cover Letter 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
