      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Linguistics Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Linguistics Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, upload a cover letter addressing relevant experience, including evidence of a commitment to student success, current vita and an unofficial transcript. For questions or to inquire about opportunities, please contact Dr. Sam Rosenthall (srosenth@oakland.edu), Department Chair Position Approval Information First Section School/College: College of Arts & Sciences Department: 0957 - Linguistics Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Psycholinguistics Name of Department Chair: Samuel Rosenthall Expected Hire Date: 08/15/2025 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Linguistics Job Description Summary: This posting is to create a pool of interested applicants from which the Department may draw as sections become open at any point in the 2025-2026 academic year. This posting may or may not result in the hiring of an applicant. Pre-employment screening includes verification of academic credentials and background check. Minimum Qualifications: PhD in linguistics and experience in teaching psycholinguistics. An active research program in psycholinguistics is preferred. Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply, upload a cover letter addressing relevant experience, including evidence of a commitment to student success, current vita and an unofficial transcript. For questions or to inquire about opportunities, please contact Dr. Sam Rosenthall (srosenth@oakland.edu), Department Chair Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located 