    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/36679": {
      "title": "CRNA Instructor of Practice",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | CRNA Instructor of Practice Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment CRNA Instructor of Practice Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, upload a curriculum vitae (CV), cover letter, a statement of teaching philosophy, contact information for at least three references, and unofficial transcripts. Questions regarding the position may be directed to Dr. Toni Glover Professor/Chair of Faculty Search, at tglover@oakland.edu. Posting Details Position Information Job Title CRNA Instructor of Practice Department 0090 - Nursing Requisition No. 0000808 Job Description Summary The Oakland University School of Nursing is seeking a highly motivated and qualified CRNA applicant to teach graduate students enrolled in the Oakland University-Beaumont Graduate Program of Nurse Anesthesia, beginning August 15, 2026. Applicants will be expected to engage in all aspects of the program, including but not limited to teaching in the classroom, clinical mentoring, guiding the development of clinical doctorate projects, and developing and evaluating curriculum. A minimum of two years in a leadership or faculty role is preferred. Candidates must be expert clinicians and able to demonstrate an ongoing commitment to service. The ability to effectively communicate and work within a team environment is essential. First consideration will be given to applicants who apply by March 15, 2026, with the continued search until the position is filled. After March 15, it is highly recommended you reach out to the committee chair via email if you are considering applying to learn where we are in the search process. Minimum Qualifications Graduation from an accredited School of Nursing and accredited School of Nurse Anesthesia. Doctoral degree ( DNP , DNAP , PhD) in nursing or related field preferred. A Master’s in nursing or related field may be accepted if the candidate is enrolled in a doctoral program and will complete the program within a year of hire. Current certification/recertification by the National Board of Certification and Recertification for Nurse Anesthetists. Must hold a current Michigan Registered Nurse license or be eligible for Michigan RN licensure and specialty licensure to practice in Michigan as a Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist. A minimum of two years of practice experience in the specialty of nurse anesthesia. Teaching experience in clinical or didactic areas is preferred. Expertise in academic or hospital administrative leadership preferred—knowledge of and familiarity with academic programs, institutions, and procedures. Experience with clinical placement and contract management preferred. Excellent organizational and analytical skills. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to communicate effectively with others. Strong organizational and time management skills. Flexibility and ability to prioritize multiple tasks in a fast-paced setting. Strong interpersonal skills consistent with demands for frequent contact with hospital and university employees, external agencies, and students are required. Self-directed and can follow standard operating procedures, but demonstrates initiative and problem-solving abilities. Demonstrated ability to automate and improve processes, and work at a high level of accuracy. Strong computer skills (Microsoft Word®, Excel®, and PowerPoint®); classroom technology knowledge (Moodle, Microsoft Office, Zoom). Must have a valid Michigan driver’s license to travel between Oakland University, Corewell Health, and affiliate site locations. Experience in evidence-based practice change and leading student DNP and research projects. Unless otherwise required by the Council on Accreditation of Nurse Anesthesia Educational Programs, the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education, the Higher Learning Commission, or an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional, and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Assists the OU-Beaumont Graduate Program of Nurse Anesthesia Program Director in the management of all aspects of classroom and clinical components of the program. Develops, implements, monitors, and evaluates classroom and clinical teaching and processes related to clinical and classroom instruction of graduate students enrolled in the program. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, upload a curriculum vitae (CV), cover letter, a statement of teaching philosophy, contact information for at least three references, and unofficial transcripts. Questions regarding the position may be directed to Dr. Toni Glover Professor/Chair of Faculty Search, at tglover@oakland.edu. School/College & Department/Program Summary The School of Nursing offers high-quality and accessible education through CCNE -accredited programs, including basic BSN , RN- BSN , BSN second degree, DNP in nurse anesthesia, acute care nurse practitioner, family nurse practitioner, adult-gerontology nurse practitioner, forensic nursing, post-master’s DNP , and a post-baccalaureate forensic nursing certification program. A new online Ph.D. program began in Fall 2019. For more information, visit the School of Nursing website: http://www.oakland.edu/nursing. More About Oakland University The University is located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University offers 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan that is dedicated to building ongoing, collaborative relationships, Oakland University embraces community and civic engagement to enhance the lives of its students and positively impact the broader community. Learn more about Oakland University’s Mission & Vision and Strategic Plan . Pay Basis Open Date 12/19/2025 Open Until Filled Yes Job Category Full-time Faculty EEO Statement Oakland University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Teaching Statement Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/36533": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Interdisciplinary Health Sciences",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Interdisciplinary Health Sciences Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Interdisciplinary Health Sciences Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, upload a cover letter addressing relevant experience, evidence of a commitment to student success, current vita, and an unofficial transcript. For questions or to inquire about opportunities, please contact Dr. Melissa Reznar (reznar@oakland.edu), MS in Interdisciplinary Healthcare Systems Coordinator Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Health Sciences Department: 1037 - Interdisciplinary Health Sciences Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Interdisciplinary Healthcare Systems Name of Department Chair: Amanda Lynch Expected Hire Date: 01/01/2026 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Interdisciplinary Health Sciences Job Description Summary: The Department of Interdisciplinary Health Sciences invites applicants for the positions of Lecturer and Special Lecturer to instruct courses in graduate level courses in the Interdisciplinary Healthcare Systems master’s program. This masters program trains students to meet competencies for healthcare practice: Patient-centered care, Interdisciplinary teamwork, Evidence-based practice, Quality improvement, Informatics, Social determinants of health. Courses cover topics including inter-professional teams and decision making; healthcare ethics; contemporary issues in healthcare; evidence-based decision making; and practicum and capstone courses. This posting is to create a pool of interested applicants from which the Department may draw as sections become open at any point in an academic year. This posting may or may not result in the hiring of an applicant. Pre-employment screening includes verification of academic credentials and background check. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree, but doctorate degree is preferred, in a discipline relevant to the course(s) taught. Preference for candidates with experience as a clinician, health care provider, or health care administration. Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply, upload a cover letter addressing relevant experience, evidence of a commitment to student success, current vita, and an unofficial transcript. For questions or to inquire about opportunities, please contact Dr. Melissa Reznar (reznar@oakland.edu), MS in Interdisciplinary Healthcare Systems Coordinator Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 11/20/2025 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, 