      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Italian Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Italian Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Approval Information First Section School/College: College of Arts & Sciences Department: 1107 - Modern Languages & Literatures Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Italian Name of Department Chair: Adolfo Campoy-Cubillo Expected Hire Date: 08/15/2025 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Italian Job Description Summary: Oakland University invites applications for the position of (Special) Lecturer of Italian Language and Culture. We seek a dynamic and committed educator to teach undergraduate in Italian language (elementary through advanced levels) and Italian culture, including literature, film, history, and contemporary issues. The ideal candidate will have a passion for student- centered teaching and demonstrate a commitment to inclusive and intercultural pedagogies. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree or higher in Italian, Italian Studies, Romance Languages, or a closely related field. Native or near-native proficiency in Italian and English. Demonstrated experience teaching Italian at the university or secondary level. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Special Instructions to Applicants: Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration,