c year. This posting may or may not result in the hiring. Pre-employment screening includes verification of academic credentials and background check. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants are required to possess native or near-native fluency in Spanish. A degree or training in Translation and Interpretation or equivalent professional certification is required. Demonstrated professional experience as a translator and interpreter in court, health care, or other professional settings is expected. A master’s degree in Spanish or a closely related field is required for appointment at the rank of lecturer. Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply, upload a cover letter addressing relevant experience, including evidence of a commitment to student success, current vita, and an unofficial transcript. For questions or to inquire about opportunities, please contact Dr. Adolfo Campoy-Cubillo (campoycu@oakland.edu), Department Chair Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 04/17/2025 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages a