    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/34287": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Studio Art",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Studio Art Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Studio Art Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, upload a cover letter addressing relevant experience and particular courses of interest to teach, a personal creative portfolio (either a single pdf or a document with the URL to link the portfolio), current vita and an unofficial transcript. For questions or to inquire about opportunities, please contact Associate Professor Meaghan Barry (mcbarry@oakland.edu) Position Approval Information First Section School/College: College of Arts & Sciences Department: 0138 - Art, Art History and Design Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Studio Art Name of Department Chair: Meaghan Barry Expected Hire Date: 08/15/2025 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Studio Art Job Description Summary: The Department of Art, Art History and Design invites applicants for the positions of Lecturer and Special Lecturer to instruct 1000- to 2000-level art courses in the Studio Art program. Courses may include art & technology, drawing, 2D and 3D foundations, painting, photography, and sculpture. This posting is to create a pool of interested applicants from which the Department may draw from as sections become open at any point in the 2025-2026 academic year. This posting may or may not result in the hiring of an applicant. Pre-employment screening includes verification of academic credentials and background check. Minimum Qualifications: MFA Degree in Art & Technology, Drawing, Painting, Photography, Sculpture or a related field. Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply, upload a cover letter addressing relevant experience and 