    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/34284": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Writing &amp; Rhetoric",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Writing &amp; Rhetoric Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Writing & Rhetoric Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. 1. A cover letter expressing teaching interests, experiences, and availability. Be sure to include the following information: a. A statement of teaching philosophy including pedagogical approach and use of technology and new media. b. Minimum and maximum number of sections desired, available/preferred days of the week, times of day, and degree of online activity. 2. A current and complete curriculum vitae with contact information; educational history (including continuing education); teaching history listing all institutions and sections taught; other relevant employment history; publications, conference attendance, presentations and relevant professional development experience. 3. Transcripts (unofficial) 4.Sample syllabi, instruction assignments, grading rubrics, student projects, or any other documents that would be helpful in illustrating your teaching approach. 5. Contact information for at least two academic professional references who are qualified to evaluate your teaching ability, including one from a writing program administrator for whom you have taught. For questions or to inquire about opportunities, please contact Dr. Megan Schoen ( meganschoen@oakland.edu ). Position Approval Information First Section School/College: College of Arts & Sciences Department: 1663 - Writing and Rhetoric Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: First Year Writing Name of Department Chair: Megan Schoen Expected Hire Date: 08/15/2025 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Writing & Rhetoric Job Description Summary: The Department of Writing and Rhetoric invites applicants for the positions of Lecturer and Special Lecturer to instruct courses in First-Year Writing. This posting is to create a pool of interested applicants from which the Department may draw as sections become open at any point in the 2025-2026 academic year. This posting may or may not result in the hiring of an applicant. Pre-employment screening includes verification of academic credentials and background check. Minimum Qualifications: Requirements are an MA degree in Rhetoric and Composition or related field (Ph.D. preferred), knowledge of composition pedagogy and teaching new media, and minimum of one year of teaching experience in a computer classroom or partially online setting. Experience with course management software such as Moodle or Blackboard is required. Special Instructions to Applicants: 1. A cover letter expressing teaching interests, experiences, and availability. Be sure to include the following information: a. A statement of teaching philosophy including pedagogical approach and use of technology and new media. b. Minimum and maximum number of sections desired, available/preferred days of the week, times of day, and degree of online activity. 2. A current and complete curriculum vitae with contact information; educational history (including continuing education); teaching history listing all institutions and sections taught; other relevant employment history; publications, conference attendance, presentations and relevant professional development experience. 3. Transcripts (unofficial) 4.Sample syllabi, instruction assignments, grading rubrics, student projects, or any other documents that would be helpful in illustrating your teaching approach. 5. Contact information for at least two academic professional references who are qualified to evaluate your teaching ability, including one from a writing program administrator for whom you have taught. For questions or to inquire about opportunities, please contact Dr. Megan Schoen ( meganschoen@oakland.edu ). Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 03/19/2025 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) List of References Optional Documents Sample Syllabus Teaching Evaluation Other Document Teaching Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
