      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Post-Doctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Post-Doctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Other requirements: (1) a 1-page letter of intent (2) a 1-page statement of commitment to engineering education and vision. (3) a 2-page statement of research vision for broadening participation in engineering. This should include details on the design and implementation of research protocols with a timeline and the framework for broadening the participation of undergraduate and graduate students in engineering. Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Engineering and Computer Science Department: 2095 - Industrial & Systems Engineering Position Title: Other Field of Specialty: Industrial and Systems Engineering or Related Disciplines Name of Department Chair: Vijitashwa Pandey Expected Hire Date: 08/01/2025 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Post-Doctoral Research Associate Job Description Summary: Focuses on advancing research in systems optimization and safety engineering and contributing to the academic and professional development goals of the department. This role includes opportunities for collaborative research, and mentorship, supporting the ISE department’s commitment to excellence in education and innovation. Minimum Qualifications: ● Completed a Ph.D. in Engineering (human factors engineering, data analytics, or manufacturing) or any area in industrial and systems engineering or closely related fields by the appointment date. ● Competency in research techniques. ● Effective oral and written communication skills for grant writing and manuscript publication. Special Instructions to Applicants: Other requirements: (1) a 1-page letter of intent (2) a 1-page statement of commitment to engineering education and vision. (3) a 2-page statement of research vision for broadening participation in engineering. This should include details on the design and implementation of research protocols with a timeline and the framework for broadening the participation of undergraduate and graduate students in engineering. Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 12/16/2024 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Other Document Other Document 2 Other Document 3 Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
