      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Journalism Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Journalism Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, upload a cover letter addressing relevant experience, including evidence of a commitment to student success, current vita and an unofficial transcript. For questions or to inquire about opportunities, please contact Dr. Kathleen Battles (battles@oakland.edu). Position Approval Information First Section School/College: College of Arts & Sciences Department: 1664 - Communication, Journalism and Public Relations Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Journalism Name of Department Chair: Kathleen Battles Expected Hire Date: 01/01/2025 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Lecturer/Special Lecturer - Journalism Job Description Summary: The Department of Communication, Journalism, and Public Relations invites applicants for the positions of Lecturer and Special Lecturer to instruct courses in journalism, including Introduction to Journalism among other courses. This posting is to create a pool of interested applicants from which the Department may draw as sections become open at any point in the 2025-2026 academic year. This posting may or may not result in the hiring of an applicant. Pre-employment screening includes verification of academic credentials and background check. Minimum Qualifications: MA in journalism or a related field; experience as a professional journalist. Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply, upload a cover letter addressing relevant experience, including evidence of a commitment to student success, current vita and an unofficial transcript. For questions or to inquire about opportunities, please contact Dr. Kathleen Battles (battles@oakland.edu). Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 12/16/2024 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
