    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/32245": {
      "title": "Physical Therapy Class and Clinical Lecturers (PT Faculty)",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Physical Therapy Class and Clinical Lecturers (PT Faculty) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Physical Therapy Class and Clinical Lecturers (PT Faculty) Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Health Sciences Department: 0070 - Health Sciences Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Physical Therapy Name of Department Chair: John Krauss Expected Hire Date: 09/04/2024 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Physical Therapy Class and Clinical Lecturers (PT Faculty) Job Description Summary: Applicants will apply as class and clinical lecturers, guest lecturers or Bridge the Gap professionals. Applicants will be paid for the hours worked at the pay rate at which they work. $30/hour for Guest Lecturer $35/hour for Bridge the Gap $30/hour for Class Lecturer $20/hour for Clinical Lecturer Class and clinical lecturers and guest lecturers will assist the instructor of record in the delivery of the course. Class and clinical lecturers will perform teaching related duties at the direction of the instructor of record. Duties may include: providing lectures, assisting in the instruction of skills, proctoring examinations, providing feedback to students and other teaching related duties as assigned. Bridge the Gap professionals will provide specialized instruction for the event. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in physical therapy, health professional field, medical field or related field of expertise. Licensed as a health professional as applicable. Special Instructions to Applicants: Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and