    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/30691": {
      "title": "Lecturer - SAT Test Preparation",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Lecturer - SAT Test Preparation Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Lecturer - SAT Test Preparation Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Approval Information First Section School/College: Academic Affairs Department: 2159 - Strategic Programs Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Education- Math or English Name of Department Chair: Lori Crose Expected Hire Date: 08/01/2024 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Lecturer - SAT Test Preparation Job Description Summary: Oakland University’s Department of Professional and Continuing Education ( PACE ) provides discounted SAT preparation courses for students and community members in partnership with Kaplan Test Prep. The prep courses are held on campus, although the program has recently expanded to include partnerships with local high schools who have requested on-site SAT prep for their students. We are looking for instructors to teach for the SAT Preparation Program, either on OU’s main campus or off-site at local High Schools. Instructors would be paid $40/hour to provide 21 hours of class instruction and to proctor 2 full-length SAT practice test (29 hours total). Instructors will also receive 1 paid hour of training from PACE to help them prepare for the course. Instructors will be provided with an extremely detailed Teacher’s Edition that goes with the book students receive as part of the program in addition to pre-designed Power Points that complement the Teacher’s Edition; instructors have the freedom to edit these materials and utilize them as they see fit. Minimum Qualifications: Certified high school teachers who have a strong grasp of high school Math and English concepts are preferred. Special Instructions to Applicants: Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University 