      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Lecturer Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Lecturer Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please indicate your area of expertise for expedited consideration. Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Education & Human Services Department: 6228 - Teaching & Learning Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Math, Social Studies, Science, or Language Arts Name of Department Chair: Danielle Ligocki Expected Hire Date: 08/01/2024 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Lecturer Job Description Summary: The Department of Teaching and Learning at Oakland University is accepting applications for part-time lecturers. The department offers programs at both the undergraduate and graduate level, including teaching preparation at the Elementary Education and Secondary Education levels, as well as MAT in Reading with a Reading Specialist Endorsement and a Ph.D. in Literacy, Culture, and Language. Our programs are well-established and internaionally recognized, and we have strong partnerships with surrounding communities and districts. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s Degree in Reading, Education, or a related field. 3 – 5 years of PK12 classroom teaching experience. Willingness to use a web-based learning management system. Familiarity with navigating video conferencing platforms, with the intent to use in some classroom settings. Ph.D. is preferred. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please indicate your area of expertise for expedited consideration. Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County,