    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/29622": {
      "title": "Wellness &amp; Health Promotion Lecturer - Env Justice PH 5350",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Wellness &amp; Health Promotion Lecturer - Env Justice PH 5350 Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Wellness & Health Promotion Lecturer - Env Justice PH 5350 Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Health Sciences Department: 1034 - Public and Environment Wellness Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Public and Environmental Wellness Name of Department Chair: Caress Dean Expected Hire Date: 11/01/2023 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Wellness & Health Promotion Lecturer - Env Justice PH 5350 Job Description Summary: Oakland University is seeking a passionate and dedicated instructor to teach an environmental justice course to Master of Public Health students. The course focuses on how environmental factors affect the health of groups and populations. The ideal candidate will have expertise in environmental justice and public health, with a commitment to equity and social justice. Responsibilities: · Develop and teach a course on environmental justice that explores the intersection of environment, health, and social inequality · Engage students in critical thinking and analysis of environmental justice issues and their impact on marginalized communities · Foster a supportive and inclusive learning environment that promotes student success · Contribute to the development and growth of the Environmental Justice program and curriculum · Address and assess the student learning outcomes stated in the syllabus, and issue timely course grades · Adhere to the general terms outlined for lecturers and follow the University guidelines for instruction and grading as stated in the university catalog. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s or Doctoral degree in Public Health, Community Health, Environmental Science, or relevant degree. Must be available to teach at Oakland University (Auburn Hills) on Wednesdays from 5:30 pm – 7:17 pm. Special Instructions to Applicants: Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 10/27/2023 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
