    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/28896": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator in Counseling",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Program Coordinator in Counseling Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Program Coordinator in Counseling Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Education & Human Services Department: 1770 - Counseling Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Counseling Name of Department Chair: Todd Leibert Expected Hire Date: 05/01/2022 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Program Coordinator in Counseling Job Description Summary: A Program Coordinator for the Department of Counseling provides clinical supervision for students enrolled in CNS 6960, Practicum in Counseling. Responsibilities for Program Coordinators include meeting with practicum students (supervisees) one time per week for one hour to review recorded clinical cases, providing clinical supervision, and reviewing all required documents. Additional requirements include following Instructor syllabi and SEHS Counseling Center policy, maintaining ongoing communication with both Instructor and the Counseling Center Coordinator, responding to emergency client situations, assisting the instructor with providing supervisee midterm and final evaluations, and maintaining ethical & professional standards as a supervisor and for supervisees. The review of applications is ongoing and continuous. Position availability varies by semester, depending on the needs of the department. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree, preferably in counseling; Relevant certifications and/or licenses; Minimum of two years of pertinent professional experience in the specialty area in which the student is enrolled; Knowledge of the program’s expectations, requirements, and evaluation procedures for students; Either received or are participating in relevant training in counseling supervision; Willingness to use a web-based learning management system; Familiarity with navigating video conferencing platforms (such as Zoom) with the intent to use in some classroom or other interpersonal settings; Special Instructions to Applicants: Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 03/16/2022 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
