      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Lecturer - Foundations of Hlth Behav &amp; Hlth Ed (PH 5000 - S23) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Lecturer - Foundations of Hlth Behav & Hlth Ed (PH 5000 - S23) Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Health Sciences Department: 1034 - Public and Environment Wellness Position Title: Lecturer Field of Specialty: Public/Community Health Name of Department Chair: Rebecca Cheezum Expected Hire Date: 04/03/2023 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: Lecturer - Foundations of Hlth Behav & Hlth Ed (PH 5000 - S23) Job Description Summary: Oakland University is searching for an Instructor to teach an online, asynchronous course on the foundations of health behavior and health education for master of public health students. This course will run July-August, 2023. The lecturer will be required to develop and deliver the assigned course based on the syllabus, address and assess the student learning outcomes stated in the syllabus, and issue timely course grades. This will be in collaboration with the program director and relevant program faculty to ensure compliance with accreditation competency requirements. The instructor of record will be responsible for adhering to the general terms outlined for lecturers and for following the University guidelines for instruction and grading as stated in the university catalog. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s or Doctoral degree in health behavior, health promotion, public health, community health, or relevant degree. Special Instructions to Applicants: Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and