    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/27435": {
      "title": "PACE Part-Time Instructor",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | PACE Part-Time Instructor Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment PACE Part-Time Instructor Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter and CV summarizing educational training and engineering experience. For questions or to inquire about opportunities, please contact Dennis Corrigan, Director of Vehicle Electrification Programs dcorrigan@oakland.edu. Opportunities will be available starting May 1, 2022. Position Approval Information First Section School/College: School of Engineering and Computer Science Department: 0050 - Engineering & Computer Science Position Title: Other Field of Specialty: EV Automotive Technology Name of Department Chair: Lori Crose Expected Hire Date: 04/04/2022 Posting Details Position Information Job Title: PACE Part-Time Instructor Job Description Summary: Be part of the electric vehicle future! Part Time Instructor Oakland University The Oakland University Engineering Institute is working closely with major automotive companies to create novel educational training modules for the revolutionary transformation to electric vehicles. We are seeking professionals to collaborate with our team and teach online short courses on electric vehicles and batteries. Oakland University is a nationally recognized research institution offering BS, MS, and PhD degrees in science and engineering. It is conveniently located in the heart of the automotive community in southeastern Michigan. Successful applicants will teach a series of short courses each totaling 45 contact hours over 6 weeks. Classes are conducted in live online remote sessions. Sessions will be 2-3 hours for 3 days a week in mornings or afternoon. Class participants are a diverse and highly motivated group of engineers from international automotive companies. Assistance with start-up course materials and online teaching will be provided. This targeted part time job is generously compensated in comparison to regular part time faculty positions. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should have strong engineering and science backgrounds (MS or PHD or equivalent) with practical multidisciplinary knowledge and experience with electric or hybrid electric vehicle engineering. We seek applicants with a strong engineering background, a commitment to excellence in teaching, and an enthusiasm for preparing automotive engineers develop automobiles for the future. Experience with online teaching is a plus. Special Instructions to Applicants: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter and CV summarizing educational training and engineering experience. For questions or to inquire about opportunities, please contact Dennis Corrigan, Director of Vehicle Electrification Programs dcorrigan@oakland.edu. Opportunities will be available starting May 1, 2022. Oakland University Standard Language Oakland University is a nationally recognized doctoral university of high research activity located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University has 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan, Oakland University is committed to building ongoing and collaborative relationships with the surrounding communities. Community and civic engagement enhances the lives of our students and has a positive impact on our broader community. Open Date: 04/21/2022 Open Until Filled: Yes Job Category: Part-time Faculty EEO Statement: Oakland University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
