    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/39313": {
      "title": "IT Financial/Budget Analyst",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | IT Financial/Budget Analyst Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment IT Financial/Budget Analyst Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title IT Financial/Budget Analyst Department 2167 - University Technology Services Position Number 988205 Requisition No. S02858 Salary Range/Pay Rate $61,728 - $65,000 annually Benefits of Working at Oakland University Oakland University offers competitive salaries and an excellent benefit program including a comprehensive medical plan with low contribution amounts for our employees, dental and vision plans at no cost for our employees, generous paid time off plans, a generous University contribution to our 403(b) retirement plan, tuition assistance for our employees and dependents, free access to our Campus Recreation Center and workout facilities, and flexible work schedules and wellness programs. These are current benefit levels subject to future changes. Oakland University offers a strong, University-wide commitment to diversity, equity and inclusion, which has garnered national recognition as a top workplace for LGBTQ+ community members; national recognition as a safe workplace, and consistent top ranking for support services to U.S. Military veteran students. Employee Group/Grade AP Band P Job Category Administrative-Professional Work Schedule FT/Reg (40 hours) Shift/Days This is a full-time position working Monday – Friday, 8am-5pm. INTERNAL APPLICANTS ONLY . First consideration will be given to those who apply by October 29, 2026. Pay Schedule Month Number of Hrs./Wk. 40 Position Information Position Information Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in finance, accounting, business administration, or a related field or an equivalent combination of education and/or experience. A minimum of two (2) years of experience in a financial skillset related to accounting, budgeting, cost analysis, forecasting, financial reporting, and/or similar experience. Strong proficiency of spreadsheets using but not limited to (MS Excel, Google Sheets, etc.) Proficiency with data analysis tools including Excel, and/or budgeting software. Excellent Microsoft and Google Workspace skills. Experience in clerical accounting/bookkeeping. Ability to analyze and track contracts along with software &amp; support renewals. Effective oral and written communication skills. Strong analytical and organizational skills. Ability to effectively collaborate with university constituents. Ability to work well with all levels of employees and understand the need for confidentiality. Ability to work under pressure. Ability to multitask. Desired Qualifications Master’s degree. Course work or certifications in Accounting. Proficiency with data analysis tools SQL , and/or advanced budgeting software. Experience in Higher Education and their accounting principles. Experience with Enterprise Resource Planning or ERP (Banner) or others. Experience in GAAP \\ Fund Based Accounting. Experience working in IT or relevant education a plus. Any experience in IT contract management and compliance. All Qualifications Unless otherwise required by an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Position Details Position Purpose The information technology (IT) Financial/Budget Analyst, reporting through the IT Business Operations department, serves as a key resource for financial planning for University Technology Services ( UTS ) at Oakland University and coordinates between technical units to help ensure the efficient and strategic planning for financial resources. Main responsibilities include: ● Coordinating directly with the CIO and IT leadership staff to develop the UTS budget ● Tracking and monitoring UTS expenditures and working to ensure purchases align with budgetary constraints and cost-saving initiatives ● Developing plans for the appropriate allocation of resources to IT departments ● Overseeing critical tasks such as cost management, funding proposals, grants management, and financial reporting ● Regularly collaborating with IT procurement, project management, and coordinators to address department needs ● Supporting UTS risk management by assessing and mitigating financial risks ● Conducting financial planning and forecasting for UTS ● Balancing monthly ledgers for UTS Working with campus departments, including University Technology Services, analyze and evaluate multi-year and long term cost projections related to total project costs for technology solutions. Job Open Date 10/15/2026 Job Close Date Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a member of the Oakland University Administrative-Professional Group? Yes No No Response Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Work Sample Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/39312": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President for Constituent Philanthropy",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Assistant Vice President for Constituent Philanthropy Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Assistant Vice President for Constituent Philanthropy Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Assistant Vice President for Constituent Philanthropy Department 7420 - Major and Corporate Giving Position Number 988867 Requisition No. S02841 Salary Range/Pay Rate $150,000 - $160,000 annually Benefits of Working at Oakland University Oakland University offers competitive salaries and an excellent benefit program including a comprehensive medical plan with low contribution amounts for our employees, dental and vision plans at no cost for our employees, generous paid time off plans, a generous University contribution to our 403(b) retirement plan, tuition assistance for our employees and dependents, free access to our Campus Recreation Center and workout facilities, and flexible work schedules and wellness programs. These are current benefit levels subject to future changes. Employee Group/Grade AP Band V Job Category Administrative-Professional Work Schedule FT/Reg (40 hours) Shift/Days This is a full-time position. First consideration will be given to those who apply by September 30, 2026. Pay Schedule Month Number of Hrs./Wk. 40 Position Information Position Information Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree or an equivalent combination of education and/or experience A minimum of six (6) years of significant achievement in a broad-based development, sales, or marketing role with demonstrated success raising gifts of $1,000,000 and above, plus two (2) years of supervisory/management experience. Knowledge of all areas of fundraising, including campaign experience with proven success in building productive, long-term relationships with university administrative and academic leadership. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Excellent organizational and analytical skills. Ability to communicate effectively with others Excellent customer service focus and ability to interact with students, faculty, staff, alumni, donors, and friends of the University. High level of commitment, trust and enthusiasm. Desired Qualifications Master’s degree. Certified Fund Raising Executive Development experience in higher education, preferably within a campaign environment. Experience in Blackbaud Fundraiser Performance Management or similar CRM . Experience developing and implementing engagement strategies through events, donor relations, communications, and other programming. Demonstrated knowledge of cultivation and alumni engagement strategies. All Qualifications Unless otherwise required by an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Position Details Position Purpose The Assistant Vice President for Constituent Philanthropy provides strategic leadership for academic and unit-based fundraising across University Advancement. This role leads and manages the academic/unit Directors of Philanthropy, strengthens philanthropic partnerships with Deans and university colleagues, and ensures that academic priorities are translated into compelling donor opportunities. The position also carries a select portfolio of top-tier prospects, with emphasis on principal, major, and complex unit-based opportunities. Job Open Date 09/17/2026 Job Close Date Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a member of the Oakland University Administrative-Professional Group? Yes No No Response Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
