    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/39309": {
      "title": "Executive Director for Enterprise Philanthropy",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Executive Director for Enterprise Philanthropy Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Executive Director for Enterprise Philanthropy Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Executive Director for Enterprise Philanthropy Department 7420 - Major and Corporate Giving Position Number 986827 Requisition No. S02838 Salary Range/Pay Rate $130,000 - $140,000 annually Benefits of Working at Oakland University Oakland University offers competitive salaries and an excellent benefit program including a comprehensive medical plan with low contribution amounts for our employees, dental and vision plans at no cost for our employees, generous paid time off plans, a generous University contribution to our 403(b) retirement plan, tuition assistance for our employees and dependents, free access to our Campus Recreation Center and workout facilities, and flexible work schedules and wellness programs. These are current benefit levels subject to future changes. Employee Group/Grade AP Band V Job Category Administrative-Professional Work Schedule FT/Reg (40 hours) Shift/Days This is a full-time position. First consideration will be given to those who apply by September 30, 2026. Pay Schedule Month Number of Hrs./Wk. 40 Position Information Position Information Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education and/or experience. Minimum of seven (7) years of significant achievement in a broad-based development, sales, marketing, corporate/foundation relations, planned giving, annual giving, nonprofit management, or related relationship-based revenue generation role. Demonstrate success securing or materially advancing gifts, grants, sponsorships, or philanthropic commitments of $500,000 and above. Previous supervisory, management, or significant program leadership experience. Knowledge of multiple areas of fundraising, including annual giving, planned giving, corporate and foundation relations, donor pipeline development, campaign readiness, and donor engagement. Proven success building productive, long-term relationships with university administrative and academic leadership, faculty, staff, alumni, donors, corporate and foundation representatives, and friends of the University. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Excellent organizational and analytical skills. Ability to communicate effectively with others and work collaboratively across multiple teams and constituencies. Excellent customer service focus and ability to interact with students, faculty, staff, alumni, donors, corporate and foundation partners, and friends of the University. Requires a high level of commitment, judgment, trust, discretion, and enthusiasm. Desired Qualifications Master’s degree. Certified Fund Raising Executive designation. Development experience in higher education, preferably within a campaign or campaign-planning environment. Experience with Blackbaud Fundraiser Performance Management or similar CRM . Experience developing and implementing enterprise philanthropy strategies involving annual giving, planned giving, blended giving, corporate/foundation relations, donor pipeline development, stewardship, and donor upgrade strategies. Demonstrate knowledge of cultivation, solicitation, proposal development, and long-term donor engagement strategies. All Qualifications Unless otherwise required by an applicable collective bargaining agreement, all minimum, additional and desired qualifications are preferred, but qualifications, degrees, and/or experience deemed comparable and/or equivalent by Oakland University in its sole and exclusive discretion may be considered. Position Details Position Purpose The Executive Director for Enterprise Philanthropy leads institution-wide philanthropic channels that support pipeline development, donor engagement, and revenue growth across University Advancement. This role oversees Annual Giving, Planned Giving, and Corporate and Foundation Relations, ensuring these functions operate as integrated enterprise strategies rather than separate channels. The position also carries a strategic portfolio tied to enterprise priorities, including planned and blended gift prospects, corporate/foundation relationships, and high-capacity non-alumni or institution-wide prospects. Job Open Date 09/17/2026 Job Close Date Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a member of the Oakland University Administrative-Professional Group? Yes No No Response Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/39300": {
      "title": "Vice Provost for Academic Affairs",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Vice Provost for Academic Affairs Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Vice Provost for Academic Affairs Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For consideration, applications should be submitted by 10/30/2026. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Vice Provost for Academic Affairs Department 2154 - Academic Affairs Requisition No. 0000843 Job Description Summary INTERNAL APPLICANTS ONLY The Vice Provost for Academic Affairs is a member of the Provost’s leadership team and supports the overall strategies of Academic Affairs as they relate to program review, accreditation and undergraduate education. The Vice Provost works with the Executive Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost, the deans of the college and schools, the faculty, the division of Student Affairs, the Office of Institutional Research, Assessment and Data Analytics and others to coordinate university accreditations and develop university-wide innovative program initiatives to streamline program review and accreditation at all levels. The Vice Provost serves as the primary university liaison for institutional accreditation, including the leadership, oversight and direction of administrative units and committees that contribute to quality assurance and accreditation. The Vice Provost coordinates efforts with the Higher Learning Commission ( HLC ) and the Michigan Association of State Universities ( MASU ). The Vice Provost provides leadership, direction and oversight of Undergraduate Education, including general education and curriculum, as well as the Bachelor of Interdisciplinary Studies program. Minimum Qualifications Tenured faculty appointment in an academic department with a minimum rank of associate professor. Earned doctorate or a terminal degree in an academic discipline and a substantial record of successful academic experience with demonstrated leadership roles. Minimum of three years of administrative experience such as department chair, unit director, program director, or associate dean. Proven record of administrative leadership and managerial experience including effective supervision of staff, creative problem solving, strategic planning, budget, project management, and organizational skills. Demonstrated evidence of supporting excellence in teaching, scholarly activity, professional development and community service. Demonstrated commitment to shared governance and academic excellence. Ability to effectively communicate and collaborate with all members of the university community and external constituencies. Demonstrated commitment to cultural diversity and the ability to work with individuals and groups from diverse backgrounds. Ability to analyze and interpret data and effectively communicate to a broader audience. Collaborative management style that fosters trust, respect, and successful working relationships with students, faculty, staff and administration. Ability to handle sensitive situations and confidential personnel matters. Evidence of successful collaboration and interdisciplinary and interprofessional work. Knowledge of academic support services and current trends in higher education. Experience in developing curricular initiatives and policies and procedures. Experience in program assessment Ability to work evenings and weekends as required. Special Instructions to Applicants For consideration, applications should be submitted by 10/30/2026. School/College & Department/Program Summary More About Oakland University The University is located on 1,443 acres of scenic land in the cities of Rochester Hills and Auburn Hills in Oakland County, Michigan. The University offers 142 bachelor’s degree programs and 138 graduate degree and certificate programs. Academics include programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, School of Business Administration, School of Education and Human Services, School of Engineering and Computer Science, School of Health Sciences, School of Medicine and School of Nursing. As an anchor institution in southeastern Michigan that is dedicated to building ongoing, collaborative relationships, Oakland University embraces community and civic engagement to enhance the lives of its students and positively impact the broader community. Learn more about Oakland University’s Mission & Vision and Strategic Plan . Pay Basis Open Date 10/14/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Job Category Academic Administrator / Dean EEO Statement Oakland University is an Equal Opportunity institution. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
